#: includes/class-bomcas-leads.php:430
#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:242
#: includes/class-bomcas-rates-admin.php:147
msgid "Income tax"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:370
msgid "Canadian income tax applies the federal and provincial brackets, the basic personal amounts, and the payroll contributions that the personal-tax file lists for employment income. Quebec includes the federal abatement. Ontario includes surtax and the health premium. British Columbia includes the tax reduction."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:371
msgid "Payroll, paycheck, and take-home pay"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:372
msgid "A Canadian cheque uses the pension and employment-insurance factors in the rate file, then the income-tax estimate divided by the number of pays. A British Columbia pay date on or after the July date stored in the dataset uses the July withholding rate from that same row, not the annual return rate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:373
msgid "Vehicle, land transfer, and mortgage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:374
msgid "Vehicle purchase uses the sales-tax rules for a dealer sale or a private purchase on the date you enter. Land transfer is estimated for British Columbia and Ontario from the published tables. The mortgage calculator uses the interest rate you type and the compounding convention you select. It does not look up a lender rate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:379
msgid "Canada Revenue Agency individual income tax rates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:383
msgid "Canada Revenue Agency GST/HST"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:393
msgid "Hide a country or a single calculator without deleting pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:395
msgid "Calculators → Toggles has a switch for Canada and a switch for each tool. Turning a tool off removes it from shortcodes and blocks. Existing pages stay published."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:396
msgid "Setup → Country focus does not change these switches. Leave both countries on when the site should offer both. The preset that creates missing pages reads this list only to decide what a shortcode may render, not which pages to insert."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:403
msgid "Edit a cell, import a sheet, and publish a new year without editing pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:405
msgid "Calculators → Rates shows one slice of a rate file: country, jurisdiction, rate type, and tax year. An empty cell does not create an override. A value you change is stored apart from the bundled file, so a plugin update does not wipe it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:407
msgid "Import and export"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:410
msgid "Export writes the current slice as CSV, Excel, or the JSON override list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:411
msgid "An import starts as a dry run. Apply it only after the row errors are empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:412
msgid "Each row needs a file name, a path such as jurisdictions/BC/0/pst, and a number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:413
msgid "JSON pasted into Import overrides replaces matching paths. It does not delete a path you leave out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:416
msgid "Pushed updates and the year in force"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:417
msgid "A signed package can be pulled when Pro is active or when Lite opt-in is saved. Your override still wins until you clear it. The year shown on pages is the newest year in the personal-tax file whose effective date is today or earlier. Year shown on calculator pages overrides that. Leave the box empty to stay automatic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:418
msgid "If the calendar year is not in the file yet, pages name the latest year as the latest on file and wp-admin shows a warning. They do not present that older year as the current calendar year. Adding the new year updates every marked page on the next view. Saving, importing, pulling, or publishing rates also clears the page cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:424
msgid "Token reference"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:426
msgid "Placeholders that become the current rate, amount, or date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:428
msgid "A token is a placeholder in curly braces. The page replaces it when someone views the page. The stored text keeps the token, so next year’s file changes the number without a page edit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:431
msgid "{year} is the year in force. {year_label} adds “latest rates on file” when this calendar year is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:432
msgid "{updated} is the month the dataset was verified. {effective} is the date those rates took effect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:433
msgid "{bpa:BC} is that province’s basic personal amount. Use FED for the federal amount."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:434
msgid "{rate:BC.income.first} and {rate:BC.income.top} are bracket rates, written as a percent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:435
msgid "{example:BC.income.42000.total} runs the engine. The 42000 is the wage you want illustrated, not a stored answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:436
msgid "{deadline:balance_due} and {source:us.federal} read the calendar and the source title in the rate file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:439
msgid "On Page content, click the field, then a token button. Hover the button for the meaning. The same tokens work in a heading, an intro, a search title, a search description, and extra sections."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:444
msgid "Page content and SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:445
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:456
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:473
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:446
msgid "Change a heading or add sections without losing them on update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:448
msgid "Calculators → Page content lists pages marked as calculator pages. Heading, intro, and button label replace those parts only. Extra sections, when Pro is active, replace the generated guide and keep your HTML."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:449
msgid "Search title and search description are used for the document title and the meta description when you fill them in. Leave them blank to keep the generated title. Put tokens in any of these fields when the sentence includes a year or an amount."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:450
msgid "Reset to default deletes only that page’s edit record. It does not delete the page. A plugin update never writes over a saved edit. If the generated guide has changed since you saved, and you did not write extra sections, the page shows a short note that a newer default exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:455
msgid "Shortcodes, blocks, and the builder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:457
msgid "Put a calculator in a page, a block, or a builder layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:459
msgid "The shortcode is [bomcas_calculator id=\"income-tax\" province=\"BC\"]. The id is income-tax, sales-tax, or mortgage-payment. The province code presets the place. Payroll and take-home pay on the Professional and Agency plans use [bomcas_calculator_pro id=\"payroll-deductions\" province=\"BC\"]. Personal does not include payroll."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:460
msgid "The block inserter lists BOMCAS Calculator. It stores the same id and place. The builder screen, when the add-on is active, lays out fields for a custom calculator. Numbers the visitor types are still not posted unless they ask for an email or a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:463
msgid "A disabled tool renders nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:464
msgid "The hero button on a managed calculator page goes to a service page, not to the contact page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:465
msgid "Managed pages keep the shortcode in the database. The long guide is added at view time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:472
msgid "Embed kit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:474
msgid "Frame a calculator on another site you control."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:476
msgid "The embed screen is part of the optional add-on. List the host names that may load the frame, one per line. The snippet is an iframe or a script tag with a signature for that host and tool. A domain that is not on the list is refused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:477
msgid "White-label can hide the credit inside the frame. The calculator still runs in the browser. Do not put a secret key in the snippet. The signature is a permission for that domain, not a licence key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:482
msgid "Leads and integrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:483
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:494
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:503
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:512
msgid "Visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:484
msgid "The email form, what is stored, and where a copy can be sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:486
msgid "The email form under an estimate is off until you enable it on the Leads screen. A lead stores the name, email, calculator, and the result the visitor chose to send. Amounts they typed stay out of the server unless that form is sent. Old leads are deleted after the retention you set. One network address can send only so many leads an hour."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:487
msgid "The consent sentence is required. Extra questions are one per line. A copy of each lead can be mailed to the notify address. Webhooks, Mailchimp, HubSpot, and Google Sheets are filled in on this screen when the add-on is active. Lite keeps the lead list either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:488
msgid "Usage counts how often a calculator is opened. It does not store the amounts. Filter the lead list by name, email, or calculator id. Delete removes that row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:495
msgid "How often each calculator is opened."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:497
msgid "Calculators → Usage counts openings. It does not record wages, prices, or other amounts the visitor typed. The overview chart uses the same counts for the last 30 days. An empty chart means nothing has been opened in that window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:504
msgid "A button, or an embedded scheduler, after a result."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:506
msgid "Set the button label, the provider name, and the URL of the scheduling page. Blank URL hides the button. Lite shows the button. The add-on can also embed the scheduler on the page. The booking URL is the page you already use. This plugin does not create appointments by itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:513
msgid "French and Spanish labels on the calculator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:515
msgid "The language switch is a control on the calculator. It changes the labels shipped with the plugin. It does not translate your page content. A switch requires the matching nonce, so a bare link cannot flip the language. Currency display can follow the locale, including es-MX with USD, from this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:516
msgid "Rate figures stay in the dataset’s units. Translating a label does not change a bracket."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:522
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:531
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:549
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:560
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:571
msgid "Site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:523
msgid "Industry landing pages you choose to publish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:525
msgid "A pack is a set of landing pages for an industry. Nothing is published until you select a pack and publish it. Publishing can replace a pack page that already exists, so leave this screen alone during an ordinary plugin update. The setup wizard can point at a pack. Choosing none leaves your pages as they are."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:532
msgid "Hide the licence and the BOMCAS name on a client site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:534
msgid "Calculators → White-label hides the licence key, the plan, and the account screen from users who are not on the allow list. Allowed user IDs are comma-separated. A capability can be used instead. An optional PIN is stored as a hash and is not shown again. People who are hidden see a short unlock form, not the key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:537
msgid "Menu label replaces the Calculators name in the left menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:538
msgid "Hide BOMCAS Canada in the plugin list when the client should not see the vendor name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:539
msgid "Agency email is used for renewal mail instead of the BOMCAS address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:540
msgid "A configuration constant can lock hiding on, so a client administrator cannot turn it off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:543
msgid "The calculators keep working while the licence is hidden. Hiding it does not delete the key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:550
msgid "An optional licence for updates. The calculators do not require one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:552
msgid "Lite runs sales tax, income tax, and the mortgage calculator with no purchase. Calculators → Account stores a licence key for the optional add-on. The key is saved on this site and is not printed in the page source afterwards. White-label can hide this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:553
msgid "The add-on keeps calculating if a subscription lapses. A licence is how the site receives add-on updates and support. It does not switch the calculators off, and it does not stop you from changing the GPL code. Plan names on the overview are Personal, Professional, and Agency. Billing itself is handled by the site that sold the licence, not by a call from this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:554
msgid "The Pro settings screen shows the update entitlement and a link to the hosted billing page when one has been saved. Pasting a key here does not charge a card."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:559
msgid "Privacy and accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:561
msgid "What stays in the browser, and how the screens are meant to be used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:563
msgid "Calculator inputs stay in the browser. They are not posted, not stored in a cookie, and not sent to an analytics host unless you separately add a measurement id. A lead or a PDF is created only when the visitor asks. The optional credit is a link you turn on. The plugin does not phone home for calculator use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:564
msgid "Trust screen"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:565
msgid "Calculators → Trust records the day you checked an official source. Do not invent that date. The public pages name the source next to the figures. Colour contrast on the admin screens uses the navy, blue, and orange palette, and form fields have visible labels. Tips are buttons that show their text on hover and on focus, so they are available from the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:570
msgid "Caching"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:572
msgid "Why a static cache must be cleared when rates change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:574
msgid "WP Fastest Cache stores a copy of the HTML. A token would otherwise stay frozen at the year that was current when the copy was made. The plugin clears that cache when you save a rate override, apply an import, pull a package, or publish a draft. WP Rocket is cleared too when that plugin is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:575
msgid "The daily job also clears the cache on 1 January and on any effective date in the personal-tax file or any sales-tax segment start. That is the day the year in force can change without anyone editing a page. If a host uses a different cache, clear the calculator pages after you import a new year."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:581
msgid "Troubleshooting and FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:582
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:605
#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:621
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:583
msgid "The checks to make before you write a support note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:585
msgid "A page still shows last year’s number"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:586
msgid "Confirm the new year is in the rate file and that its effective date is today or earlier. Clear the page cache. A buyer’s extra sections are shown instead of the generated guide, so those sections need tokens if they name a year."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:587
msgid "A calculator is blank"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:588
msgid "Check Toggles. A disabled tool renders nothing. Confirm the shortcode id is one of the shipped tools and the place code matches the file, such as BC or CA."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:589
msgid "A calculator page was not created"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:590
msgid "Country focus does not create them. On the add-on’s preset screen, use Add the next few pages. Each click adds a few missing pages and skips any address that already exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:591
msgid "The hero button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:592
msgid "It opens a service page for that kind of work. It does not open the contact page or the calculator page itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:595
msgid "Does the plugin store what a visitor types? Only if they send the email form or download a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:596
msgid "Can I show a credit? Yes. Settings has one unchecked box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:597
msgid "Will an update replace my page text? No. Saved edits stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:604
msgid "Changelog"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:606
msgid "What changed in this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:608
msgid "1.0.5"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:609
msgid "Shorter calculator heroes, a long guide under each calculator, and figures that come from the rate dataset through tokens. This guide was added. Saving rates clears the page cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:610
msgid "1.0.4"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:611
msgid "Overview chart for the last 30 days. Settings screens use one label-above form. Activation does not create or edit pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:612
msgid "1.0.3"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:613
msgid "Guide-page layout and one-sentence descriptions. Rate tables stay in the plugin unless an administrator opts in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:614
msgid "1.0.2 and earlier"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:615
msgid "1.0.2 put the calculator before the rate table. 1.0.1 used the banner artwork. 1.0.0 shipped sales tax, income tax, and the mortgage payment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:620
msgid "Support notes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:622
msgid "Record a problem on this site. Nothing is sent to a ticket service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:624
msgid "Write the subject and what happened. The note is stored in this site’s database and a copy is mailed to the WordPress administrator address. The form does not call an outside help desk. Include the page address and the calculator id. Do not paste a secret key or a visitor’s full return."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-docs.php:625
msgid "Read Troubleshooting first. Many blank calculators are a toggle, a shortcode id, or a cached page."
msgstr ""

