msgid "Built by BOMCAS Canada"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:25
msgid "Owned by Dellendo Farquharson. Every figure is an estimate from the rate file. It is not a filing, a ruling, or a Canada Revenue Agency service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:27
msgid "Lite calculators"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:31
msgid "Pro calculators"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:32
msgid "The Pro add-on is a separate plugin. Lite does not prompt for it, lock a control, or install it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:32
msgid "See Pro"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:52
msgid "Does this file a return?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:53
msgid "No. The figures are estimates. They are not a filing, a ruling, or a Canada Revenue Agency service. The plugin does not prepare a T1, a T2, a T4, or a remittance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:56
msgid "Where do the typed numbers go?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:57
msgid "The arithmetic runs in the browser. The form is not posted for the calculation. A view count is stored on your own WordPress site. An email, a PDF, or a Google event is sent only after you turn that option on and, for email or PDF, the visitor submits it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:60
msgid "Which tax year does income tax use?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:61
msgid "The newest year in the personal tax file whose start date is today or earlier. The file shipped with Lite is the 2026 personal tax year. A later file, imported under Calculators, Rates, is used on the next page view. Sales-tax segments in the file run from 2022 through 2026, and the date the visitor picks selects the segment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:64
msgid "Which places are covered?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:65
msgid "Canadian income tax and sales tax cover the federal tables and all 13 provinces and territories. Some Pro tools cover fewer places, and those limits are named on each calculator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:68
msgid "Does Lite include Canadian payroll?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:69
msgid "No. Canadian payroll deductions and salary after tax start on the Professional plan. Personal does not include them. Lite income tax does use the CPP, CPP2, EI, QPP, and QPIP amounts from the rate file when it works out credits. It does not show a paycheque."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:72
msgid "What do the Pro plans cover?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:73
msgid "Personal is one site, Professional is five sites, and Agency is twenty-five sites. Prices are in Canadian dollars on the pricing page. The licence is for updates and support while it is active or in grace. The GPL code you already installed keeps running if the subscription ends."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:76
msgid "How do I put a calculator on a page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:77
msgid "Add the BOMCAS Tax Calculators – Canada block, or the shortcode [bomcas_calculator id=\"income-tax\" province=\"ON\"]. Pro tools use [bomcas_calculator_pro id=\"payroll-deductions\" province=\"ON\"]. The province code is optional. Income tax and sales tax default to British Columbia."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:80
msgid "Which WordPress version does it need?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:81
msgid "Lite requires WordPress 6.2 or newer. Pro requires WordPress 6.5 or newer, because it declares Lite as a required plugin. Both require PHP 7.4 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:84
msgid "Does it work with my theme?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:85
msgid "Yes. The calculator is a block and a shortcode. It does not replace your theme, your header, or your styles outside its own form. It has been checked on the Accountants Expert theme and on a default block theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:88
msgid "Does it work in the block editor?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:89
msgid "Yes. Search the block inserter for BOMCAS Tax Calculators – Canada. Choose income tax, sales tax, or a mortgage payment, and optionally a province. Payroll blocks are not in Lite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:92
msgid "Can I use a shortcode instead of a block?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:93
msgid "Yes. Paste [bomcas_calculator id=\"sales-tax\" province=\"BC\"] into a shortcode block or the classic editor. The ids in Lite are income-tax, sales-tax, and mortgage-payment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:96
msgid "Does it work with Elementor, Beaver Builder, or another page builder?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:97
msgid "Yes, where the builder can place a WordPress block or a shortcode. Use the builder’s shortcode widget if it does not list the block. The calculation still runs in the visitor’s browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:100
msgid "Does it work on WordPress Multisite?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:101
msgid "Yes. Activate it on the sites that should show a calculator. A Pro licence counts each site address you activate. Network activation is supported. Each site still needs its own activation on the licence if you use Pro updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:104
msgid "How accurate are the numbers?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:105
msgid "They follow the rate file shipped with the plugin, or a file you import later. Income tax uses federal and provincial brackets, basic personal amounts, and the CPP, CPP2, EI, QPP, and QPIP amounts in that file. They are estimates for a conversation, not a assessed return."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:108
msgid "How do rate updates work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:109
msgid "Lite ships the rates in the plugin. A new tax year arrives when you update the plugin from WordPress.org. You can also import a file under Calculators, Rates. A remote download stays off until you opt in on that screen, and it sends no calculator inputs. Pro, with a saved licence key, checks accountantsexpert.com once a day. A failed signature or checksum leaves the bundled rates in place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:112
msgid "Can I replace a rate myself?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:113
msgid "Yes. Calculators, Rates exports the current file and imports a replacement. An override you saved stays in place if a later file touches the same value, and the screen tells you when that happens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:116
msgid "Does it send calculator inputs to Google?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:117
msgid "No, unless you save a Google measurement id. With that field empty, nothing is sent to Google. The arithmetic does not leave the browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:120
msgid "What about email and PDF?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:121
msgid "Both stay off until you enable them. A visitor has to submit the form before an email is sent or a PDF is requested. The calculation itself is not that submission."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:124
msgid "What does the site store?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:125
msgid "A view count on your own site. Leads, if you turn the form on, are stored in your database and can be deleted on a schedule you set. Calculator inputs used only for the estimate are not posted to Accountants Expert."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:128
msgid "What does Lite include?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:129
msgid "Three calculators: Canadian income tax, GST, HST, PST and QST, and a mortgage payment. The styling shipped with the plugin. The rate file in the zip. Lite does not include payroll, corporate, savings, or property tools, white-label, a site-count licence, or a Pro download."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:132
msgid "Is Lite a trial that locks features?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:133
msgid "No. Lite is the free plugin. Pro tools are not hidden inside it. Limits are the tools Lite simply does not include. Upgrade prompts appear in wp-admin only, and a visitor never sees them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:136
msgid "How do I upgrade from inside the plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:137
msgid "Open Calculators, Account and upgrade. Plans and any active coupon come from the store. Buy sends this site address and the receipt email only after you check the consent box, then opens Stripe Checkout and returns to the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:140
msgid "Will Lite install Pro for me?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:141
msgid "No. After you buy, open My Account on accountantsexpert.com, download the Pro zip, and upload it under Plugins, Add New. Paste the licence key into Pro."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:144
msgid "How many sites does a plan cover?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:145
msgid "Personal is 1 site, Professional is 5, and Agency is 25. Lite itself is not limited by a site-count licence. The count applies to Pro updates and support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:148
msgid "How do I activate or remove a site?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:149
msgid "Pro shows the sites on the licence. My Account on accountantsexpert.com is where you activate or deactivate this site, see invoices, and change the plan. The plugin stores the licence key locally and does not print it back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:152
msgid "When does a plan renew?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:153
msgid "On the renewal date shown in Pro and in My Account. Monthly, quarterly, and yearly prices are the amounts Stripe charges for that period. You can turn renewal off. Access continues until the period you already paid for ends."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:156
msgid "Can I cancel, and is unused time refunded?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:157
msgid "You can cancel renewal at any time from My Account. Cancellation stops the next charge. Unused time in a period you already paid for is not refunded, except where the law requires it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:160
msgid "Do coupons work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:161
msgid "Yes, when the store has an active coupon. The upgrade screen and the pricing page list coupons that have banner text and are still inside their dates and redemption cap. An empty list means there is no public promotion. You can still type a code at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:164
msgid "What does support cover?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:165
msgid "Pro support and updates run while the licence is active or in grace. Lite is the free plugin. Support for a paid plan is from the store, at the address in My Account. The calculators keep running if a subscription lapses. A lapsed licence pauses updates and support. It does not switch the installed code off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:168
msgid "What is white-label?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:169
msgid "Professional and Agency can hide the licence key, plan, and upgrade screens from users who are not on an allow list. Personal does not include white-label. Lite does not include it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:172
msgid "Which languages ship with Lite?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:173
msgid "English, French (Canada), and Spanish. The calculators use the language of the WordPress site when a translation is installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:176
msgid "Does the form fit a phone?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:177
msgid "Yes. The calculator form fits a narrow screen. The gallery includes an income-tax view at phone width. That is the layout that was checked, not a separate mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:180
msgid "Where do I paste the licence key?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:181
msgid "In Pro, on the licence screen. Leave the licence server empty on the store itself. On a customer site, set it to https://accountantsexpert.com. The key is saved on that site and is not shown in the page source afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:184
msgid "What happens if I do not enter a licence?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:185
msgid "Pro calculators still run. Updates and support stay paused until the licence is active or in grace. Lite never asks for a key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:188
msgid "How do I pay?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:189
msgid "Stripe Checkout. You can pay by card, and by Apple Pay or Google Pay where Stripe offers them. Accountants Expert does not store card numbers. Prices are in Canadian dollars."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:192
msgid "How does Quebec work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:193
msgid "Income tax includes the federal abatement and the Quebec workers deduction. Sales tax can show QST. Payroll tools, on Professional and Agency, use RRQ, RQAP, and the Quebec withholding table where that calculator has a row. The salary-versus-dividend table does not include Quebec."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:196
msgid "Does land transfer tax include Toronto?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-bomcas-listing.php:197
msgid "Land transfer tax is a Pro tool. British Columbia and Ontario use the brackets in the file. A Toronto checkbox adds the municipal tax. Manitoba, New Brunswick, Nova Scotia, and Prince Edward Island use a rate you type. Quebec uses brackets you type. A blank rate means no tax is added."
msgstr ""

